{"causes": ["The profound social and economic inequalities of the French Ancien Régime fueled widespread discontent among the Third Estate, which Mirabeau effectively articulated.", "The intellectual ferment of the Enlightenment, particularly ideas on popular sovereignty and constitutionalism, provided the philosophical bedrock for Mirabeau's political arguments.", "Mirabeau's own tumultuous personal life and experience with arbitrary imprisonment under lettres de cachet instilled in him a fervent commitment to individual liberty and legal reform."], "effects": ["Mirabeau's powerful oratory and strategic leadership significantly influenced the transformation of the Estates-General into the National Assembly in 1789.", "His death in April 1791 removed a key moderating voice from the French Revolution, contributing to its subsequent radicalization and the eventual rise of the Jacobins.", "Mirabeau's advocacy for a constitutional monarchy, though ultimately unsuccessful, shaped early debates on executive power and legislative authority in revolutionary France."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "honore-gabriel-riqueti-comte-de-mirabeau", "sourceName": "Honoré Gabriel Riqueti, comte de Mirabeau", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "french-revolution", "targetName": "French Revolution", "context": "Mirabeau was a leading figure in the early stages of the French Revolution (1789-1791), serving as a dominant voice in the National Assembly."}, {"sourceSlug": "enlightenment", "sourceName": "The Enlightenment", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "honore-gabriel-riqueti-comte-de-mirabeau", "targetName": "Honoré Gabriel Riqueti, comte de Mirabeau", "context": "Enlightenment ideals of liberty, reason, and constitutional governance deeply influenced Mirabeau's political philosophy and proposals for reform in France."}, {"sourceSlug": "honore-gabriel-riqueti-comte-de-mirabeau", "sourceName": "Honoré Gabriel Riqueti, comte de Mirabeau", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetS